        "content": "# Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n## Architecture\n\n### Approach\nBuild a lightweight YAML syntax validator using custom parsing logic. The validator will check for structural correctness of YAML content without fully parsing it into objects (no dependency on `js-yaml` or similar libraries).\n\n### Validation Strategy\nSince we cannot add dependencies, we'll implement a rule-based validator that checks for:\n1. **Indentation consistency** - mixed tabs/spaces, inconsistent indent levels\n2. **Quote matching** - unclosed single/double quotes\n3. **Colon syntax** - mapping values require space after colon\n4. **Bracket/brace matching** - flow sequences and mappings\n5. **Basic structure** - detects obviously malformed lines\n\n### Module Design\n\n```\nsrc/\n  yaml-validator.ts       - Core validateYaml() function + types\n  yaml-validator.test.ts  - Unit tests\n  validate-yaml.ts        - CLI entry point\n```\n\n### Types\n\n```typescript\ninterface YamlValidationError {\n  line: number;\n  column: number;\n  message: string;\n}\n\ninterface YamlValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  errors: YamlValidationError[];\n}\n```\n\n### CLI Design\n\n```\nbun run src/validate-yaml.ts <file-path>\n```\n\n- Reads file from argv[2]\n- If no arg and stdin is piped, reads from stdin\n- Prints \"Valid YAML\" to stdout on success (exit 0)\n- Prints errors to stderr on failure (exit 1)\n\n### Package.json Script\n\nAdd: `\"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"`\n\n## Constraints\n- Zero new dependencies\n- Bun built-in file I/O only (`Bun.file()`, `process.stdin`)\n- Follow existing camelCase/PascalCase conventions\n"
