        "content": "# Tasks: YAML Validator Command\n\n## Implementation Tasks\n\n### T1: Create YAML validator core module\n- **File**: `src/yaml-validator.ts`\n- **Status**: pending\n- **Description**: Implement `YamlValidationError` and `YamlValidationResult` types, and the `validateYaml(content: string): YamlValidationResult` function with rule-based checks for:\n  - Mixed tabs and spaces in indentation\n  - Inconsistent indentation levels\n  - Unclosed quotes (single and double)\n  - Missing space after colon in mappings\n  - Unmatched brackets `[]` and braces `{}`\n  - Duplicate keys at the same indentation level\n\n### T2: Create YAML validator tests\n- **File**: `src/yaml-validator.test.ts`\n- **Status**: pending\n- **Description**: Write comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Valid YAML strings (simple key-value, nested, lists, multi-line)\n  - Invalid: bad indentation\n  - Invalid: unclosed quotes\n  - Invalid: missing space after colon\n  - Invalid: unmatched brackets/braces\n  - Invalid: duplicate keys\n  - Edge cases: empty string, comments only, blank lines\n\n### T3: Create CLI entry point\n- **File**: `src/validate-yaml.ts`\n- **Status**: pending\n- **Description**: CLI script that:\n  - Reads file path from `process.argv[2]`\n  - Falls back to stdin if no file arg and stdin is piped\n  - Calls `validateYaml()` on content\n  - Prints \"Valid YAML\" to stdout and exits 0 on success\n  - Prints errors to stderr and exits 1 on failure\n\n### T4: Update package.json with validate-yaml script\n- **File**: `package.json`\n- **Status**: pending\n- **Description**: Add `\"validate-yaml\": \"bun run src/validate-yaml.ts\"` to scripts. Do NOT add any new dependencies.\n\n## Summary\n- Total tasks: 4\n- Implementation tasks: 4\n- Doc tasks: 0\n"
