        "content": "# Design: YAML Validator Command\n\n## Overview\nAdd a YAML validator command to the existing CLI. The validator uses a hand-written YAML syntax checker (no new deps) that validates common YAML constructs.\n\n## Architecture\n\n### Approach: Hand-written YAML Syntax Validator\nSince we cannot add new dependencies, and Bun does not ship a built-in YAML parser, we will implement a lightweight YAML syntax validator that checks for common syntax errors:\n- Indentation consistency (spaces only, consistent width)\n- Unclosed quotes (single and double)\n- Invalid mapping syntax (missing colon after key)\n- Duplicate keys at the same level\n- Tab characters (not allowed in YAML)\n- Unterminated multi-line strings\n\n### File Structure\n```\nsrc/\n  yaml-validator.ts       - Core validation logic (validateYaml function)\n  yaml-validator.test.ts  - Unit tests\n  index.ts                - Updated to route \"validate-yaml\" subcommand\n```\n\n### Core Interface\n```typescript\ninterface YamlValidationResult {\n  valid: boolean;\n  error?: string;\n  lineNumber?: number;\n}\n\nfunction validateYaml(input: string): YamlValidationResult;\n```\n\n### CLI Flow\n```\nindex.ts\n  ├── (no args / non-validate-yaml) → existing greet behavior\n  └── \"validate-yaml\" subcommand\n       ├── read file from argv[3]\n       ├── call validateYaml(contents)\n       ├── valid → print success, exit 0\n       └── invalid → print error + line number, exit 1\n```\n\n### Validation Rules (in order)\n1. **Empty check**: Empty/whitespace-only input → valid (empty YAML document)\n2. **Tab check**: Scan for tab characters used for indentation → error\n3. **Line-by-line parsing**:\n   - Check quote balance (single/double quotes must be closed on same line unless multi-line scalar)\n   - Check mapping syntax (`key: value` patterns)\n   - Check indentation consistency (must use spaces, consistent within blocks)\n   - Check for common structural errors (e.g., `- ` list items vs mapping items at wrong indent)\n\n### Error Messages\nFormat: `Error on line {N}: {description}`\n\n## Constraints\n- Zero new dependencies\n- Pure TypeScript, runs with Bun\n- Follows existing code patterns (camelCase functions, kebab-case files, co-located tests)\n"
